Lieve Mieke,

Today marks eleven years since our paths first crossed. Eleven years since a small moment in Wageningen quietly started an _Entdeckungsreise_ - an exploration I could never have planned.

I still smile when I think about how it began. That lunch meeting where we first saw each other - a seemingly ordinary moment. And yet somehow it created just enough familiarity for us to easily talk again a few days later at that party. I didn’t know it yet during lunch, but that evening something shifted for me. _Dat was het moment dat ik oprecht verliefd op je werd_ - with your kind heart, your curiosity about the world, your exploratory nature, and of course, your smile.

Looking back now, it feels like we have been travelling together ever since. 

Not only across countries - though we certainly did a fair share of that. Recently I tried to look up what our very first trip together was. I went through my photos and it seems that Stockholm might have been the first real holiday we took together. (Although there is a mysterious gap in my photos in 2015, so maybe I’m missing something!) But the Sweden trip I remember vividly. Kayaking together through the water around Stockholm - discovering the city from the water, quietly gliding along side by side. _Heerlijk._ I loved that.

Over the years we have taken so many journeys together. Through snowy mountains, across oceans, into tiny houses, and into entirely new chapters of life. Some adventures were big and wild, others small and quiet. But some of my favourite journeys are still the conversations we have had along the way - in bars at night, during long drives, or simply sitting somewhere talking about life. _Diese tiefen Gespräche genieße ich in vollen Zügen._

In our vows I once called you my true north. And I still feel that today. When life gets confusing or the path ahead becomes foggy, you are the safe harbour that gently guides me back.

Lately, I feel something beautiful returning again. I am truly proud of you for exploring again, for searching again, for allowing yourself to discover new directions. I love seeing that spark. And I love that somehow we seem to have more time again - or maybe simply more energy - for the kind of deep conversations that have always been such an important part of us.

And yet I also love the very practical journeys we navigate together. Managing life. Getting things in order. Building our little world step by step. I felt that so strongly while we were figuring out schools for Felien. I was genuinely happy doing that with you - thinking things through together, making decisions together, shaping the environment in which our daughter will grow. _Thuis komen doe ik het liefst vol enthousiasme bij jullie._

Being a parent with you is one of the greatest adventures of my life. I love watching you as a mother. I love building this family together with you. And I love being by your side as your partner.

Sometimes our life together feels like a long expedition. We carry maps, snacks, laughter, chaos, and occasionally the question: “Are we actually doing this right?” But somehow we always find the next path forward. And when storms appear - as they inevitably do on any long journey - I still trust what we promised each other: that love, truth, and trust will guide us through them.

And now another little traveler may soon join our expedition.

I look forward to that deeply. To welcoming another little human into this strange and beautiful journey we are on together. I will admit that sometimes I also feel a little scared about how we will manage it all. Life already feels full and intense. But the truth is: I do want this journey with you.

Also… I have to say: the way you recently seduced me into slowing down was very impressive. Just a candle, a conversation, and gently pulling me away from the laptop. Honestly, that was seduction level 103. I did not stand a chance. And I loved it. 😉

Mieke, if the last eleven years have taught me anything, it is that the most meaningful journeys are rarely the ones we carefully plan. They are the ones we walk together, discovering the path step by step. You are still the explorer I most want beside me.

- For the next mountains.
- For the next oceans.
- For the next quiet conversations in the middle of the night.
- And for the next little travelers who may join our path.

Hand in hand, still discovering. And perhaps many years from now we will look back again at this moment and smile - remembering that it all began with a simple lunch in Wageningen, and two people who decided to keep walking in the same direction.

_I love you._ \
_Ik hou van je._ \
_Ich liebe dich._

Mario ❤️
